# What Tor proves

Tor proves the far end of the circuit holds the key the address encodes, so the
bytes reached the service you meant. It does not say who the CapTP peer is: the
peer is whoever holds the local socket that service forwards to.

The accepting side learns nothing about who dialed it. CapTP does not need
to know, because what a caller may do depends on the references it holds,
not on who it is.

A three-party [handoff]($link.page('concepts')) is the exception. It relies on
the location a peer declared,
and an accepted circuit has nothing to check that declaration against, so
glowcap reports it as unproven. An [iroh]($link.page('transports/iroh'))
session can report a proved peer, because QUIC authenticated the node id.

# Bare onion locators

The service id already says where to dial, so glowcap sends onion locators
without hints. The one exception is a give to a peer already known to run glowcap,
which keeps its hints. The Goblins release glowcap pins cannot dial an onion locator that
carries hints, even though the OCapN locator rules say hints never change
which peer an address names. Hints on a locator glowcap receives are ignored rather than
refused.

The hello can still carry hints, which is how a peer states a preferred wire
profile. Live Goblins accepts a hinted hello and ignores the hints
(`zig build goblins-onion` checks this every run), so two glowcap peers over
Tor can agree on `glowcap-next`, glowcap's own experimental CapTP version. The dialer asks for it when it was handed the
glowcap form of the address, and an acceptor configured for it answers the
same way. Every other session, including every session with a Goblins vat,
uses the baseline.
[ADR-0042](https://github.com/jimisaacs/glowcap/blob/main/docs/decisions/adr/ADR-0042-onion-interoperability.md)
records the locator rule and how a dialer picks glowcap's own profile only
when it knows the other side is glowcap.

[Choosing a transport]($link.page('transports/choosing')) puts onion beside the
others. [What you can depend on]($link.page('stability')) lists the live Tor
checks and known gaps.
